<%args>
</%args>

<div class="container" style="max-width: 1100px;">
  <div style="text-align:center; padding: 25px 0 10px 0;">
    <img src="/static/img/seedquest_logo.png" style="max-width: 360px; width: 100%; height: auto;" />
  </div>

  <h3>What is SeedQuest?</h3>
  <p>
    SeedQuest is a professional digital platform for agricultural analysis,
    field trials, and breeding support.
    It is designed for agronomists, breeding teams, and agricultural companies
    working with data-driven decision-making.
  </p>

  <p>
    The platform integrates field experiments, phenotypic observations,
    yield and quality data, climatic inputs, and agronomic parameters
    into a structured and auditable workflow.
  </p>

  <h3>How is SeedQuest used?</h3>
  <p>
    SeedQuest is used to design and manage field trials,
    evaluate crop performance across locations and seasons,
    and support professional agronomic consulting and breeding programs.
  </p>

  <h3>What crops are supported?</h3>
  <p>
    SeedQuest is actively used for maize, soybean, sunflower, wheat,
    and other major field crops, with flexible support for custom trial designs
    and crop-specific ontologies.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 20px; font-size: 12px; opacity: 0.75;">
    SeedQuest is built on open scientific tools developed within the Sol Genomics Network (SGN) ecosystem.
  </p>
</div>
